{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":13879,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"e68c38fb-c98c-51ba-af09-b07f215a6a27","total_cost_usd":0.21990200000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8012,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":1078,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8012,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8012},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4752,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004837,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1078,"cacheReadInputTokens":905,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8012,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.215065,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"The declared independent-unit column reactor_id is consistent with the frozen data: the 60 rows come from exactly 10 reactor_id values (R01-R10), each appearing 6 times (run days 7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42), and each reactor_id maps to exactly one carbon_source, with 5 reactors in the methanol arm and 5 in the glycerol arm; no reactor appears in both procedure arms.\",\"The issue is demonstrated in the selected report itself: the report states 60 measurement rows from 10 bioreactors with 6 sampling occasions per bioreactor, the Analysis section states 'Each sampling-day measurement in the file was entered as one observation', and the [selected-result] line reports a Welch two-sample t test 'on the 60 measurement rows' with df = 53.3 and n = 30 per group. This shows repeated measurements from the same independent unit (6 per reactor) were entered into a row-independent procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) as if independent, inflating the effective sample size from 5 per arm to 30 per arm.\",\"The workflow confirms the report: analysis.py appends every row's value to the per-source sample and passes the pooled 30-vs-30 vectors to stats.ttest_ind with no per-reactor aggregation or mixed/clustered modeling, so the p < 1e-12 conclusion treats non-independent rows as independent.\",\"The minted lock's unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['reactor_id'], matching the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: reactor_id' extracted in the translation receipt (extracted_token 'reactor_id', a column present in the logical header), and both v1 and v2 translation lanes minted locks from that same declaration.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declared independent-unit column reactor_id is consistent with the frozen data: the 60 rows come from exactly 10 reactor_id values (R01-R10), each appearing 6 times (run days 7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42), and each reactor_id maps to exactly one carbon_source, with 5 reactors in the methanol arm and 5 in the glycerol arm; no reactor appears in both procedure arms.","The issue is demonstrated in the selected report itself: the report states 60 measurement rows from 10 bioreactors with 6 sampling occasions per bioreactor, the Analysis section states 'Each sampling-day measurement in the file was entered as one observation', and the [selected-result] line reports a Welch two-sample t test 'on the 60 measurement rows' with df = 53.3 and n = 30 per group. This shows repeated measurements from the same independent unit (6 per reactor) were entered into a row-independent procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) as if independent, inflating the effective sample size from 5 per arm to 30 per arm.","The workflow confirms the report: analysis.py appends every row's value to the per-source sample and passes the pooled 30-vs-30 vectors to stats.ttest_ind with no per-reactor aggregation or mixed/clustered modeling, so the p < 1e-12 conclusion treats non-independent rows as independent.","The minted lock's unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['reactor_id'], matching the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: reactor_id' extracted in the translation receipt (extracted_token 'reactor_id', a column present in the logical header), and both v1 and v2 translation lanes minted locks from that same declaration."]},"ttft_ms":6084,"ttft_stream_ms":1506,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":12719,"uuid":"9f9c0b61-e302-4ccb-bafc-196117cc1225"}
